# ============================================================================
# NotationBrowser -- pick a target from the Omnis notation tree
# ============================================================================
#
# WHAT IT DOES
#   A modal picker that lets you browse the whole Omnis notation hierarchy
#   ($root -> $libs -> library -> $classes/$windows/.. -> objects/methods/..)
#   in a lazy-loading tree and return the notation path of the chosen node.
#   Used by the ExecutorConsole's "Target..." button to set a target by hand.
#
# MAIN FEATURES
#   - Tree (trNotation)      : expands on demand via $appendNodes; each node holds
#                             an item reference to the real notation object in its tag.
#   - Path display           : the selected node's $fullname is shown in dNotationPath.
#   - Filter checkbox        : hide / show #-system classes ($checkSystemClasses).
#   - Select (pbSelectTarget): returns the chosen path to the caller and closes.
#
# HOW THE RETURN WORKS (callback)
#   $construct(pExpandToPath, pCallbackRef) opens the tree expanded to a path and
#   stores pCallbackRef.$ref -- a REFERENCE to the caller's callback method (it is
#   held, NOT executed). Clicking a node sets iNotationPath = node.$tag().$ref.$fullname.
#   pbSelectTarget then calls iCallbackRef(iNotationPath) and closes the window, so
#   the caller (ExecutorConsole.$setTargetPathCallback) receives the picked path and
#   runs it through its target-resolution apparatus.
# ============================================================================

Set reference iCallbackRef to pCallbackRef.$ref ## hold a REFERENCE to the callback method (do not call it)
Calculate iInitialized as kTrue
Do $cinst.$initTree
# expand the tree and select pExpandToPath as the current node
If [pExpandToPath].$lib()
	Do $cinst.$expandTo(pExpandToPath,iTreeRef,iTreeRef) Returns node
Else
	# default: show at least the libraries
	Do $cinst.$expandTo('$root.$libs',iTreeRef,iTreeRef) Returns node
End If
Do iTreeRef.$setcurrentnode(node)
Quit method